            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I measured the performance impact using the following snippet and after 25 events, measured 0.004ms. It seems likely it's fast enough that you can't measure it accurately with the built-in timer, since it's one branch.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.g.count = 0\r\nvim.g.duration = 0\r\nlocal active = false -- tried varying this, didn't affect perf so luajit isnt inlining\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('TextChangedI', {\r\n\tcallback = function()\r\n\t\tlocal start = vim.loop.hrtime()\r\n\t\tif not active then\r\n\t\t\tlocal final = vim.loop.hrtime()\r\n\t\t\tvim.g.duration = vim.g.duration + (final - start) / 1000000\r\n\t\t\tvim.g.count = vim.g.count + 1\r\n\t\tend\r\n\tend,\r\n})\r\n```",
