            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I measured the performance impact using the following snippet and after 25 events, measured 0.004ms.\r\n\r\n25 events of `TextChangedI` is only typing 25 characters. Combined with `TextChanged` and `ModeChanged`, the number goes up considerably during the Neovim session. In general, limiting the usage of `ModeChanged`, `TextChanged` family, and `CursorMoved` family of autocommands is a good design.\r\n\r\nBesides:\r\n- I got the equivalent of 0.013ms per 25 events (after 132 events of random typing). I imagine the numbers are even higher for older machines.\r\n- This benchmark doesn't account for the overhead from built-in Neovim's machinery needed to actually call the autocommand.\r\n- This change doesn't *really* ensure that autocommand from 'mini.snippets' is created before autocommands from 'blink.cmp' and/or 'nvim-cmp'. As the order in which plugins are loaded depends on the user who can lazy load beyond reasonable doubt. Not everyone will use 'lazy.nvim' and 'dependencies' field with standalone 'mini.snippets'.",
