        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I got the equivalent of 0.013ms per 25 events (after 132 events of random typing). I imagine the numbers are even higher for older machines.\r\n\r\nIt's worth emphasizing that we likely can't accurately measure the duration since it's so short. We're likely measuring the overhead of grabbing and storing the time. I don't have an easy way to measure the overhead in neovim but I'd imagine it's negligible. \r\n\r\n> This change doesn't really ensure that autocommand from 'mini.snippets' is created before autocommands from 'blink.cmp' and/or 'nvim-cmp'. As the order in which plugins are loaded depends on the user who can lazy load beyond reasonable doubt. Not everyone will use 'lazy.nvim' and 'dependencies' field with standalone 'mini.snippets'.\r\n\r\nTotally agree, perhaps we should bring up the idea of a priority system for autocmds in the neovim repo?",
